A||||9||TigerFiero||What can I do to keep my car running cooler?||||5||
Z||000000||TigerFiero||03-01-2001||09:02 PM||||I have an 86 GT that I drive over 50 miles a day, 5-6 days a week.  From my house to work and back, and it is almost all interstate.  It seems that it wants to start to run hot after about 15 miles at 75 mph.I have flushed and serviced the cooling system and checked the fan to make sure it works.  But to get it to come on I have to turn on the air.  If I do this then my gas mileage goes to crap. Can someone give me some ideas on what to do?<P>------------------<BR>TigerFiero<BR>86 Coupe<BR>86 GT<BR>North Florida/South Georgia Fieros||||reg||5
Z||000001||2xsess||03-01-2001||09:38 PM||||First you need to find out why the fan doesn't come on with the temp instead of havig to turn the A/C on.<BR>A quick fix would be to install a switch inside that turns on the fan. Kind of tacky though.<P>I know everyone is going to ask this, did you burp the cooling system?<P>And you do realize that the fan isn't supposed to come on until I reaches 220<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">       <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>Visit My Website</A><p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 03-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||03-01-2001||09:58 PM||||Put in one of Rodney Dickman's low temp fan switches. Check the bottom of this page under  parts vendors||||reg||1
Z||000003||hugh||03-01-2001||10:01 PM||||As a temp. fix you can unplug the compressor clutch and turn on the air.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||03-01-2001||10:22 PM||||Get your radiator rodded out.  After I flushed and filled my coolant my temp stays stable even after 100 miles at about 85 mph.  You could also hook up a manual fan switch so you can run the fan whenever you want without using the AC.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||AL||03-01-2001||10:33 PM||||i would clean the radiator and also check why the fan doesn't come on,then i would put this on and your cooling problems are solved. <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=522257&a=11032114&p=38388718&Sequence=0&res=high">  <P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Sleeper||03-01-2001||10:46 PM||||you know all that black material in the engine compartment on the sides(it's under the hood on most cars)?  well if you pull all that out it adds cooling because that material keeps heat in the engine compartment.<BR><P>------------------<BR>85 GT<BR>17" Racing Hart C5 wheels, Kumho Ecsta Supra 712 tires, Intrax lowering spring, KYB shocks, KYB-GR2 struts, Chris West's Strut Tower Bar, J.E.T. super chip, Accel Super Coil, Accel Wires, K&N filter and Optima Battery.||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||03-02-2001||06:14 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Sleeper:<BR><B>you know all that black material in the engine compartment on the sides(it's under the hood on most cars)?  well if you pull all that out it adds cooling because that material keeps heat in the engine compartment.<P>Yep, I threw all of it out. 175* fan switch, 160* thermostat. stays at about 1/4 of temp gage even over 100+ ....and I have V6 turbo<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 03-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||VISCERAL||03-02-2001||11:29 AM||||A bottle of "WaterWetter" by Redline. Our local PepBoys have them for about $6. It's pink and you add it to your antifreeze. Drops temps about 15-20 degrees for a couple months(3-4). Takes longer for temps to get up high. Also use a 180 thermostat, a Rodney Dickman fan switch, and run Synthetic Mobil 1.<P>------------------<BR>Patrick Szewczyk<BR>1987 Fiero GT<BR>Silver, 5 spd, sunroof centerforce dualfriction clutch, Koni's all around, Ground Control coilovers in the rear, lowered 2" - susp.tech springs-front, poly bushings: control arms-sway bars-cradle-motor-dogbone, rear sway bar, pioneer cd player, 180 stat, 176-166 fan switch, MSD Coil, Rodney Dickman's short shifter, bushings, etc..., grand am brakes all around, k&n filter, Mustang rear scoop, next year V-8 + lowered spindles + 17x8 and 17x9" Mas Italy wheels +  235/45/17 and 255/40/17's + new paint+ custom hood vents + Mr. Mikes leather interior + 11.25" brakes w/ parking brake.||||reg||1
Z||000009||terryk||03-02-2001||11:46 AM||||Before you throw all of this at your car randomly, is it really over heating? Is it boiling over? Is the temp lamp on? Is the gauge in the red zone? Does it come down in temp once the the load is removed from the engine? The fans are set high for a reason.<P>To me, it sounds like it's more of a "feeling" rather than a fact that it's over temperature. <P>"Seems that it wants to start ...." has an "almost pregnant" sound to it.<P>There may be nothing wrong. Give us more details as to why you think something is amiss.<P>TK||||reg||1
